.\" c17.1 -- maux's stub for the POSIX c17(1) utility, which this
.\" tree does not provide. An original page (this project's own
.\" text), so it carries no third-party notice -- MIT like the code,
.\" same posture as env.1/man.1. Recorded in docs/POSIX-GAPS.md sec
.\" 5 ("Not applicable, and why") so the omission is not re-
.\" litigated. Rendered at build time to build/man/C17.TXT and
.\" staged on the play image as /usr/man/C17.
.TH C17 1 "September 17, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
c17 \- invoke a standard C compilation
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I C17
is not provided on maux.
there is no C compiler on maux; nas(1), as(1), and ld(1) are
this system's own assemble-and-link toolchain.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
as(1), ld(1)
